## Result in one paragraph

The two questions are now answered separately on the production path and the
answers are **different**, which is the point. **(a) Lattice: yes.** Every one
of the five words is in the production `SPAN_SHORTLIST` shortlist of its own
resegmentation span. **(b) Production dedup pool: no** — 0 of 18,824, measured
through the public library API at default settings and now asserted by a test
anyone can re-run from this branch. The exact rejecting site is named below,
and it is *not* a budget that is too small: the search is **emission-bound, not
pop-bound**, so widening the traversal makes it strictly worse, and that was
measured. This item ends as a **priced negative result** plus a landed general
change that makes the claim re-runnable (`Generator::generate_pool`), not as a
landed change that emits the alignment. It also found a **second, independent
blocker** that no emission work can remove.

