## Goal

Answer, on the **production** approximate path and with no wider budget
anywhere, the question that three successive fronts have each answered
differently: for `It's just a stupid game`, is the alignment whose
resegmentation is `hits justice dupe hid came` ever a candidate that
`madgab --approximate --top 50` could print, and if not, the exact
production condition that prevents it?

Then either land a **general** change that makes the production search emit
it, or deliver an implementation-ready specification with the budget
arithmetic for the recommended design.

## Why this item exists: the evidence has flipped three times

The durable fact is not any single measurement, it is that this
repository's measurements on this question have reversed three times,
always in the same direction, and always because a *scratch harness with a
wider budget* was mistaken for the production path:

| source | claim | why it was wrong or right |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [w-7b41d2](w-7b41d2.md) (14:10Z pass) | phrase absent from the pool | correct for the production binary |
| [w-04f83f](w-04f83f.md) | five words survive the shortlist, lost to the objective at 0.8199 vs 0.9295 | reachedability evidence came from a **wider-budget harness**; the production path never proposes the candidate, so no reweighting can put it in the set. Retracted. |
| [w-c4d7e8](w-c4d7e8.md) | canonical **is** in the pool: 40,546 five-word alignments contain `dupe`, best at rank 130 | scratch **exhaustive** enumeration of 1,545,903 alignments; the production search's emission budgets never reach that alignment. |
| [w-9c6f2b](w-9c6f2b.md) (agent `9c6f2b`, on `39f4e41`) | canonical **absent** from the production dedup pool: 0 of 18,824, and still 0 of 18,917 with the per-word similarity axis | measured on the **production** path with the release binary |

So the production measurement is the two most recent ones and they agree,
while the two that disagreed with them were both off-path. This item
exists to settle the question once, on the path that decides the
itinerary, and to leave behind a *procedure* that stops it being
re-derived wrongly a fourth time.

## Context, measured on the production path at `39f4e41`

- `Hits Justice Dupe Hid Came` is generated for `It's just a stupid game`
  by **no** configuration of the production search that has been tried.
- Its best admissible alignment costs 1.1195 of the 1.5 budget with cuts
  `[3,10,13,15,19]`, and under the real final scorer scores 0.7999-0.8199
  against a rank-50 cutoff near 0.8978 (both figures to be re-measured, not
  copied).
- The per-word similarity axis on `madgab-objective-axes` moved the best
  `dupe`-bearing clue from raw rank 2575 to 2017 and the best
  unrepresented-structure candidate from 188 to 122, and the canonical
  clue was still absent. Two objective axes together are worth at most
  +0.1200 against a +0.0979 gap, and the **relative** rank-50 cutoff rises
  with the change, so the objective is the wrong lever.
- At `top_n` 50 the selector's per-structure share cap is **inert**: the
  printed top 50 already contains 17 members of one structure against a
  cap of `50 / STRUCTURE_FLOOR(3) = 16`, which means the cap is already
  exceeded and the visible list is effectively the score-ranked prefix.
  The printed 50 shows 12 distinct structures as a *consequence* of score
  ranking, not as an independent diversity filter.

## Method: the production path is the only admissible evidence

This is the fence that matters most, and it exists because it has already
cost this repository three reversals.

- Every claim must be reproducible from the **release binary at default
  configuration** (`./target/release/madgab --approximate --top 50 ...`) or
  from the public library API at its default settings. State which.
- A scratch harness that widens any of `SPAN_SHORTLIST` (160),
  `SEGMENTATION_KEEP` (256), `LEXICAL_COMBINATIONS_PER_SEGMENTATION` (64),
  `LEXICAL_BRANCH_STAGE_GROWTH` (4), `LEXICAL_HEAP_POP_LIMIT` (4000),
  `LEXICAL_GLOBAL_EMISSION_BUDGET`,
  `LEXICAL_GLOBAL_POP_BUDGET`, `EMIT_PROFILE_RESERVE` (16) or the total
  cost budget **may not be cited as evidence about the production path**.
  It is legitimate to use such a harness to learn what the lattice
  *contains* — that is a different question and must be labelled as one.
- `MADGAB_TRACE_PHRASES` is an existing trace facility, not a new
  env-var knob. New knobs and `eprintln!` probes must stay on `scratch/*`.
- The two questions must be reported separately and every time:
  **(a) is the alignment in the lattice?** and **(b) is it in the
  production candidate pool?** A "yes" to (a) with a "no" to (b) is the
  expected and useful answer, and it localises the work to emission.
- If a measurement needs a rebuilt binary to be trusted, force the rebuild
  and say so. `git bisect` on this tree is untrustworthy without one,
  because boundary commits are docs-only and cargo reuses the previous
  binary — that mistake has already produced a bogus "first bad commit is
  a docs commit" conclusion.

## Fences

- No phrase-specific hard-coding, and no special case for these two
  sentences, their clues, their words, or any substring of them. Any
  production-code mention of them is a defect even in a comment.
- No `zz*` probe file, no `eprintln!` probe, no new env-var knob and no
  phase timing on the branch that reaches the accumulation branch.
- Do not re-open a cost, pronunciation, dictionary, `GAP_COST`,
  `LEXICAL_BRANCH_KEEP` or `SEGMENTATION_KEEP` front as a *number*: those
  are closed by measurement in [w-c4d7e8](w-c4d7e8.md),
  [w-1c3e77](w-1c3e77.md), [w-6f2b18](w-6f2b18.md),
  [w-7b41d2](w-7b41d2.md) and [w-b2e5c4](w-b2e5c4.md). What is open is
  **coverage**: why the emission budgets allocate their budget where they
  do, and whether a budget-derived allocation that provably reaches
  alignments of this class exists at the current wall clock.
- Do not relax, re-baseline or `#[ignore]` a test to make something pass.
  `approximate_output_is_locked` will change if the objective moves; if it
  moves, re-measure it on the merged tree and record the before/after
  honestly. In particular, do not describe a re-locked list as unchanged
  when any phrase in it differs.
- Canonical case 1 must not regress: `wreck a nice beach` must remain in
  the printed proposal set for `recognize speech`.
- `cargo fmt` and `cargo clippy` do not exist on this host; do not report
  them as run. See [../../environment-notes.md](../../environment-notes.md).
  `git` is only on `PATH` via `$GUIX_PROFILE/bin` — export it first, or
  every git command fails with "not found", which has already been
  misdiagnosed as an outage once.

## Completion criteria

- [ ] Questions (a) and (b) are each answered for the canonical
      five-word alignment on the production path, on the tree being handed
      over, with the exact release-binary or public-API command recorded.
- [ ] If (b) is "no": the **exact** production site is named — file, line,
      the quantity compared, the value that rejects the candidate, and the
      arithmetic that makes the budget binding. "The budget is too small"
      is not an answer; the site and the value are.
- [ ] Either a landed general change that makes the production search emit
      the alignment within the current interactive wall-clock budget, or
      an implementation-ready specification (exact lines, per-design budget
      arithmetic against measured `39f4e41` timings, one recommended
      design, and what the change costs in pool size). Measurement-only is
      not an acceptable end state; a *priced* negative result is.
- [ ] A regression test expresses the coverage property in general terms,
      with no example phrase in the assertion, and it fails before the
      change and passes after.
- [ ] `cargo test --release --lib`, `--test corpus_integration`,
      `--test exact_determinism` and `--test approx_determinism` are all
      run and their exact results recorded, including which acceptance
      tests pass and which do not.
- [ ] Branch `madgab-emit-coverage` is **pushed**, the working tree is
      clean, and HEAD is on that named branch and not a detached HEAD.
- [ ] This item is updated with objective state, validation, blockers and
      the next action.

